DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("sqrt((8/(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("7/(((cos(x))^2+1*(5-x)+1))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("({-8, -7, -6, -3, 2} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, -7, -6, -3, 2})) U {-9, 5}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-9, 5} U {-8, -7, -6, -3, 2} U {-8, -7, -6, -3, 2}");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("{-8, -7, -6, -3, 2} U ({-9, 5}) U {-9, 5} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, -7, -6, -3, 2})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-2, -1} U {-1, 9, 10} U {-2, -1} U {-1, 9, 10}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({-2, -1} - {-2, -1})");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-1, 9, 10} U {5, 7} U {-1, 9, 10}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`12+7*11`]? [_____]{Real(89.)}
---

What is the value of [`2/3+6/18`]? [_____]{Formula('1')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-2, -1\}`]
- [`B = \{-1, 9, 10\}`]
- [`C = \{5, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup B \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, 5\}`]
- [`B = \{-8, -7, -6, -3, 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B \cap B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`B \cup (A) \cup A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 6, -8, -7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 4, -6, 6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -6, -10, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, -8, -7>") x Compute("<-6, -10, -5>")}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, -10, -5>") . Compute("<4, -6, 6>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<6, -8, -7>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, -10, -5>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-6, -10, -5>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, -10, -5>") x Compute("<4, -6, 6>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 7, 1, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -7, -10, 6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 9, -9, 7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -9, 7>") x Compute("<7, 1, 10>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 1, 10>") x Compute("<-7, -10, 6>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, -10, 6>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<9, -9, 7>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>5)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>5)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
